        "original_id": "5b519b7c-8e22-5484-8494-7977667a2bf0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: 79 Pall Mall, Pall Mall, London\n- People: Nell Gwyn, King Charles II of England and Scotland\n- Concepts: Grade II listed building, blue plaque\n\nFacts:\n- Nell Gwyn, also spelled Gwynn or Gwynne, was born on 2 February 1650 and died on 14 November 1687.\n- Nell Gwyn was a long-time mistress of King Charles II of England and Scotland.\n- After retiring from the stage, Nell Gwyn occupied a brick townhouse that formerly stood on the site of 79 Pall Mall.\n- A blue plaque at 79 Pall Mall notes that Nell Gwyn had occupied the earlier townhouse on the site.\n- 79 Pall Mall is a Grade II listed building on Pall Mall in London.",
